<section id="pilot" class="pilot-section" aria-labelledby="pilot-title">
  <div class="shell pilot-layout">
    <div class="pilot-copy"><div class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot"></span> HELP SHAPE WHAT COMES NEXT</div><h2 id="pilot-title">A better view<br> starts with<br> <span class="serif">your store.</span></h2><p>We're looking for clothing brands to help shape Sellora. Tell us a little about your store and register your interest in the pilot.</p><span class="pilot-note">Shopify first. Starting in Pakistan.<br> No store access is granted by this form.</span></div>
    <div class="pilot-form-wrap">
      <% if flash[:notice] %>
        <div class="form-notice" role="status" tabindex="-1" data-controller="form-feedback"><span aria-hidden="true">✓</span><h3>You're on the interest list.</h3><p><%= flash[:notice] %></p></div>
      <% else %>
        <%= form_with model: @pilot_request, scope: :pilot_request, url: pilot_requests_path(anchor: "pilot"), data: { turbo: false }, html: { class: "pilot-form" } do |form| %>
          <h3>Join the pilot</h3><p class="form-intro">A few details. A useful conversation to start.</p>
      <p class="local-review-note">Local pilot interest form — requests are stored in this app’s database for review. Not a public launch.</p>
          <% if @pilot_request.errors.any? %>
            <div class="form-errors" role="alert" tabindex="-1" data-controller="form-feedback"><strong>Your request hasn't been saved.</strong><ul><% @pilot_request.errors.each do |error| %><li><% if error.attribute == :base %><%= error.message %><% else %><a href="#pilot_request_<%= error.attribute %>"><%= error.full_message %></a><% end %></li><% end %></ul></div>
          <% end %>
          <div class="form-fields">
            <div class="form-field"><%= form.label :name, "Your name" %><%= form.text_field :name, required: true, maxlength: 100, autocomplete: "name", placeholder: "Full name", aria: { invalid: @pilot_request.errors[:name].any? } %></div>
            <div class="form-field"><%= form.label :email, "Work email" %><%= form.email_field :email, required: true, maxlength: 254, autocomplete: "email", placeholder: "you@yourbrand.com", aria: { invalid: @pilot_request.errors[:email].any? } %></div>
            <div class="form-field"><%= form.label :store_url, "Store URL" %><%= form.url_field :store_url, required: true, maxlength: 2048, autocomplete: "url", placeholder: "https://yourstore.com", aria: { invalid: @pilot_request.errors[:store_url].any? } %></div>
            <div class="form-field"><%= form.label :platform, "Store platform" %><%= form.select :platform, PilotRequest::PLATFORMS, { prompt: "Select your platform" }, required: true, aria: { invalid: @pilot_request.errors[:platform].any? } %></div>
          </div>
          <p class="form-privacy" id="form-privacy">We use these details to assess your request and contact you about the pilot. <a href="#privacy">How your details are handled</a>.</p>
          <%= form.button type: "submit", class: "button button-dark", aria: { describedby: "form-privacy" } do %>Request to join <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span><% end %>
          <p class="micro">Pilot timing, availability and pricing are not yet finalized.</p>
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
      <details id="privacy" class="privacy-details"><summary>Pilot request privacy <span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>This pilot interest form collects only your name, work email, store URL and platform, together with the submission time. We use these details to assess pilot interest and follow up. Submitting does <strong>not</strong> connect a store or collect traffic, customer or order data.</p><p>Submissions are retained for local pilot evaluation and deleted on request or when the pilot ends. This build is for local review only and is not a public launch. To request deletion of a submission stored in this environment, contact the person who invited you to review Sellora (no separate public privacy inbox is published for this local build).</p><p>No email is sent by this form. There are no advertising or analytics trackers on this page; Rails uses a session cookie for form security and the submission confirmation. Basic request throttling temporarily uses your IP address in the server cache. See also <code>docs/privacy-retention.md</code> for uninstall and retention notes.</p></details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
